+The chain-rule identity at fixed `η`, `F_γ|η=J(F,G)/G_π`, has first possible
+order 29, since `G_π` has leading term `30η^-29`. Thus the coefficients
+at 22 and 25 are nonzero constants, which p.150 explicitly retains.
